A||||4||86SE||New suspension parts?  Noticeable?||||5||
Z||000000||86SE||08-30-2000||06:19 PM||||I'm pretty sure at least my front shocks are factory, not 100% sure about the rear struts.  I'm thinkin about buying KYB's, they are supposed to be better then stock.<P>Konis would be nice, but about $200 a pair, when I could get complete set of KYB's for less than that.<P>Anyone have KYB or Koni shocks?? How do they feel?<P>I have the $$ for a 3.4 conversion + small suspension upgrade, just need to know the best suspension for me to get, I don't race the car so I don't need race suspension, too stiff.<P>Opinions please!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Yellow Fiero<BR>Special Rally Heavy Duty Suspention||||reg||5
Z||000001||mrfiero||08-30-2000||07:30 PM||||If your shocks and struts are factory originals then you really need to change them out!!  Any good quality shock or strut will make an improvement, but KYB's or KONI's will really tighten things up.<P>I am partial to KYB's due to their "better bang for the buck".  As you said, you can get a complete set of KYB's for less than a pair of KONI shocks.....and unless you race your Fiero, KONI's are a little overkill.  KYB's are also about the same or even cheaper than factory replacements, so why not get a little better shock for your money?<P>Go ahead and get the KYB's....I guarantee you'll like them.||||reg||10
Z||000002||webbee||08-30-2000||08:55 PM||||I agree with mrfero. The Koni's are too expensive/stiff, unless you race. The KYB is the best bang for the buck. Nice ride. Go for it. Poly bushings, motor mts, and stabel ends are excelant too!<p>[This message has been edited by webbee (edited 08-30-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||08-31-2000||02:58 AM||||The answer is simple.<BR>Street/daily driving = KYB (I have them)<BR>Street/Strip/racing = KONI<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||1FST2M6||08-31-2000||08:26 AM||||i loved my Konis but they take a week or so to get where they really work like their suposed to... fiddeling with valving. ask GT Bastard... he seems happy with them.. try <A HREF="http://www.shox.com" TARGET=_blank>www.shox.com</A>  i got my Eibachs and Konis for $618 including shipping. i liked the konis for LOOOOONG trips... say from atlanta to sioux falls, cause you can open them up and have a squishy old mans caddy ride. or break your teeth handeling when you get there to show off...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 08-31-2000).]||||reg||1
